			"date": "2026-10-22T13:17:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@rauschma\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>rauschma</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I do this with the “Save Tabs URLs” add-on that exports tabs to a scratchpad. There are similar ones for better formatting .. but all of them re-open pasted URLs, too.</p><p>You place them in your knowledgebase or just a mail draft and prepend the current date (though the draft would have that, too). With a searchable title, this is easy to get back to. Also: my mail drafts are synched, so I can open them on any machine.</p><p><a href=\"https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/save-tab-urls/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firef</span><span class=\"invisible\">ox/addon/save-tab-urls/</span></a></p>",
